Today, I solved LeetCode 704 – Binary Search.

After working with recursion and different array techniques, today’s problem was a great reminder of how efficiently we can search a sorted array without checking every element.

💡 Approach: Binary Search using Recursion

I used a recursive binary search approach:

Find the middle element.
If nums[mid] == target, return its index.
If nums[mid] < target, search in the right half.
Otherwise, search in the left half.
If st > end, the target doesn't exist, so return -1.

The key idea is that every step eliminates half of the remaining search space.

⏱️ Time Complexity: O(log n)
💾 Space Complexity: O(log n) due to recursive calls.

